  "notes": "Projection paper (concept) for an electrostatic storage ring. Fig.4 shows projected sensitivities for axion-electron coupling (left) and axion-nucleon coupling (right), plus dark photon. Mass range 1e-19 to 1e-9 eV. No numerical data points are given in tables or text; only a plot with axis ranges. Coupling type ambiguous between AxionElectron, AxionNeutron, and DarkPhoton; demonstrator's first result targets axion-electron. No extractable numerical limit values. | Vision: Left panel of Figure 4 shows g_aee vs m_a. The lower boundary traced corresponds to the existing experimental bounds (gray curves: torsion pendulum, comagnetometer, long-range) which represent the actual constraints. The red and blue lines are projected sensitivities for the proposed experiment, not actual exclusions. The boundary traced approximates the envelope of the existing constraint curves. y-axis units GeV^-1 retained as plotted (g_aee); note this is a derivative coupling normalized differently than dimensionless g_ae. | CV axis calibration: x-min corrected 1e-19->4.75295e-21; CV axis calibration: x-max corrected 1e-09->217268; CV axis calibration: y-min corrected 1e-11->1.2881e-12; CV axis calibration: y-max corrected 1e-05->0.00637662; | Curve traced by classical CV | Calibration: Vision calibration: \u00d71e-1 (factor=1.00e-01, reason=spot-check verify/stage2, raw_ratio=0.19)",
